# Terraform state — may contain secrets in plaintext, and belongs in the remote backend.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/

# `.terraform.lock.hcl` is deliberately NOT ignored, and used to be. It is the only committed
# file that names the provider version CI actually ran against: `~> 5.0` in required_providers
# permits every 5.x, and the lock is what makes two people resolve the same one. Ignoring it
# here while the Azure and GCP trees committed theirs meant the AWS roots were the two of seven
# that could not be reproduced — the pin looked enforced and was not.

# Real variable values. Only the .example files are committed.
terraform.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars

# Plan output — can contain sensitive values.
*.tfplan

# Built Lambda packages.
build/
*.zip

# Python bytecode. Committing it churns the diff on every test run and ships stale
# artifacts into a zip if the build ever stops staging from a clean directory.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/

crash.log
crash.*.log
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json
